{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-curated ground truth: the novels each author actually wrote, supplied by the fork owner.",
    "Novels only - no short-story collections, no anthologies the author merely contributed to,",
    "and no posthumous assemblies from unpublished manuscripts. Co-authored novels ARE included,",
    "and appear under every credited author.",
    "",
    "'aliases' records the title Open Library actually stores where it differs from the published",
    "title. Open Library drops the 'Dune:' marketing prefix from the prequels and omits subtitles.",
    "This is domain knowledge, not a test workaround - the two strings name one book.",
    "",
    "Two kinds of book are excluded from the recall denominator, for different reasons, and the",
    "distinction is kept sharp on purpose - neither is a book our own filtering lost:",
    "",
    "  'unavailable'    - Open Library has no record at all, verified by direct title search.",
    "  'noLanguageData' - Open Library has the book but records no language for it, so the",
    "                     language=eng query necessarily drops it. Confirming these against",
    "                     /works/{key}/editions.json was tried and fails: that endpoint has no",
    "                     language for them either. See the note in OpenLibraryProvider.",
    "",
    "Both cap achievable recall and are the argument for a second IBookMetadataProvider."
  ],
